  "instructions": [
    {
      "primary_message": "This recipe makes about 16 cups of stew or 8 (2-cup) servings.\n\n",
      "secondary_message": null
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Slice sausage crosswise into ½-inch thick pieces.\n\n",
      "secondary_message": "3 (14 oz) pkg smoked sausage"
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Preheat a large pot over medium-high heat.\n\n",
      "secondary_message": null
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Once the pot is hot, add oil and swirl to coat the bottom. Working in batches, add sausage and cook, stirring occasionally, until golden, 4-5 minutes. Using a slotted spoon, remove sausage to a paper towel-lined plate. (Reserve pot with drippings for later use.)\n\n",
      "secondary_message": "2 tbsp extra virgin olive oil"
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Meanwhile, wash and dry the fresh produce.\n\n",
      "secondary_message": "½ small bunch cilantro\n1 lime"
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Peel and medium dice sweet potatoes. Place in a medium bowl.\n\n",
      "secondary_message": null
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Trim, seed, and medium dice bell peppers. Add to the bowl with the sweet potato.\n\n",
      "secondary_message": null
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Peel, halve, and small dice onions; peel and mince garlic. Add both to the bowl.\n\n",
      "secondary_message": "6 clove garlic"
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Return pot (with drippings) to medium-high heat, add more oil, and swirl to coat the bottom. Add veggies and spices; cook, stirring occasionally, until softened, 8-10 minutes.\n\n",
      "secondary_message": "1 tbsp extra virgin olive oil\n2 tbsp chili powder\n1 tbsp cumin, ground\n2 tsp paprika\n1 tsp salt\n¾ tsp black pepper"
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Meanwhile, mince 2 chipotle peppers. Place in a small bowl, along with 2 tbsp adobo sauce, and set aside. (Reserve remaining chipotles and sauce for another use.)\n\n",
      "secondary_message": "1 (7 oz) can chipotle peppers in adobo sauce"
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Drain and rinse beans.\n\n",
      "secondary_message": "2 (15 oz) can pinto beans\n1 (15 oz) can black beans"
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "When the veggies are softened, add cooked sausage, minced chipotles, adobo sauce, beans, broth, tomatoes, and corn to the pot. Stir to combine the stew and bring to a boil. Once boiling, reduce heat to low and simmer, stirring occasionally, until beans are tender and stew is thickened, about 30 minutes.\n\n",
      "secondary_message": "4 cups chicken or vegetable broth\n2 (14.5 oz) can fire-roasted diced tomatoes\n2 cups frozen corn"
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "While the stew is cooking, shave cilantro leaves off the stems; discard stems and mince the leaves.\n\n",
      "secondary_message": null
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "When the stew is done, juice lime into the pot, add cilantro, then stir to combine. Remove from heat.",
      "secondary_message": null
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "To serve, divide stew between bowls and enjoy!",
      "secondary_message": null
    }
  ],
